# Factory authority is repository content (2026-09-17 policy flip).
#
# Doctrine: `.factory = TRACKED BY DEFAULT`. The Factory coordination
# substrate (epic board, ACT contracts, ACT evidence, per-epic detail
# files, gate summaries, upstream triage) is durable engineering record
# that travels with the repo. New ACTs and their evidence directories
# are picked up by a plain `git add` — no per-ACT whitelist edit needed.
#
# The single exception is `.factory/tmp/`, which is the
# explicitly-local-only subtree for raw captures, machine-local probes,
# tool caches (bun-cache / bun-tmp), huge generated artifacts
# (e.g. live-userdata copies, node-gyp scratch), and any file that may
# carry secrets by accident. Everything else under `.factory/` is
# source-of-truth project content and stays tracked.
#
# Replaces the previous DEFAULT-DENY + per-ACT whitelist policy that
# had accumulated hundreds of `!/.factory/acts/...` / `!/.factory/evidence/...`
# exceptions. That policy made the canonical link from epic-board rows
# to ACT bodies fragile (every new ACT required a `.gitignore` edit
# before it could be staged) and pushed raw/scratch files into the
# same namespace as canonical evidence.
#
# See `.factory/epic-board.md` 2026-09-17 entry for the full rationale.
/.factory/tmp/
.bun-tmp/
.bun-install/

scripts/__pycache__/
